   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>I studied the GLM regression algorithms and found this wonderful site</div><div>in which Mike Kane and Brian W. Lewis describe some variants to the</div><div>ILRS algorithms which use various methods to increase the efficiency</div><div>and speed of the GLM regression:</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://bwlewis.github.io/GLM/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://bwlewis.github.io/GLM/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463007857000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ByrL2CZvYP_QgsraOu6Pm\">http://bwlewis.github.io/GLM/</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Suppose I would do in STAN, considering the QR factorization (only scratch)</div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><pre style=\"padding:8px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(229,229,229);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;font-size:17.92px;border-radius:5px;overflow-x:auto;background:rgb(248,248,248)\"><pre style=\"padding:8px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(229,229,229);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;font-size:17.92px;border-radius:5px;overflow-x:auto;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"color:#000\">    g      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> family</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$linkinv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    gprime </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> family</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">eta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    z      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> t </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">b </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> gprime<br>    W      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">gprime</span><span style=\"color:#660\">^</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> family</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$variance</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    s_old   </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> s<br>    C   </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> chol</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">crossprod</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> W</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    s   </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> forwardsolve</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> crossprod</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">W</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    s   </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> backsolve</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    t      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> Q </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%*%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> s</span></pre><pre style=\"padding:8px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(229,229,229);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;font-size:17.92px;border-radius:5px;overflow-x:auto;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"color:#000\">increment_log_prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">));</span></pre></pre></div></code></div><br>I would cut the loop and let the optimization part to STAN. Instead of working at the real data, this algorithm works on the QR</div><div>part. </div><div><br></div><div>Pre-work done in the transformed data section:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;font-size:17.92px;padding:8px 15px;border-radius:5px;border:1px solid rgb(229,229,229);overflow-x:auto;background:rgb(248,248,248)\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> s </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> t  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  QR </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> qr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">A</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  Q  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> qr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">QR</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  R  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> qr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">R</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">QR</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></pre></div></code></div><br>What I want to know, before I change the R code into STAN: Is this possible in STAN?</div><div>Or does the HḾC struggle with this approach?</div><div><br></div><div>Andre</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
