   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Monday, December 7, 2015 at 2:08:38 PM UTC-5, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">andre.p...@googlemail.com</a> wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">What I want to know, before I change the R code into STAN: Is this possible in STAN?<div>Or does the HḾC struggle with this approach?</div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>Stan doesn&#39;t have any IRLS optimization algorithms. Also, anything where the QR decomposition has to be invoked every time the log-posterior is evaluated is going to be slow because you have to call qr_Q() to get Q and qr_R() to get R. However, we are starting to do some reparameterizations using the QR decomposition (once) in regression models, not because it executes quickly but because it changes the posterior geometry in much the same way that the Matt trick does.<br><br>Ben<br><br><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "90ADoUJBAQAJ",
   "from": "andre.p...@googlemail.com",
   "author": "71c315ee557ff234",
   "date": "2015-12-08T10:27:54Z",
   "subject": "Re: Pre-STAN QR Factorization to increase speed and efficiency of STAN?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Ben,<div><br></div><div>I thought using QR before and outside of STAN. The QR-variant of IRLS calculates the QR decomposition before the loop, solves</div><div>the QR problem and transfers the solution of the QR back by re-substitution. So I would do in STAN.</div><div><br></div><div>Andre</div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "-cN7vV1FAQAJ",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2015-12-08T11:43:08Z",
   "subject": "Re: Pre-STAN QR Factorization to increase speed and efficiency of STAN?",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Tuesday, December 8, 2015 at 5:27:54 AM UTC-5, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">andre.p...@googlemail.com</a> wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I thought using QR before and outside of STAN. The QR-variant of IRLS calculates the QR decomposition before the loop, solves<div>the QR problem and transfers the solution of the QR back by re-substitution. So I would do in STAN.</div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>That can be done, but it will make little difference in optimization problems that are solved by LBGFS with Stan. It is a good idea for MCMC or meanfield ADVI if you don&#39;t have informative priors on the regression coefficients.<br><br>Ben<br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
